# Engineering Quality Standard

- Never use quick fixes, hacks, or feature downgrades to address issues.
- Always implement or repair the complete, intended functionality as described in requirements, design docs, or existing contracts.
- Avoid temporary workarounds (e.g., toggles, silent catches, or partial implementations) that reduce reliability, security, or maintainability.
- Preserve public APIs and contracts unless the change is explicitly part of the task; if changes are necessary, update all usage sites and tests accordingly.
- Prefer refactoring and adding tests to ensure robust, long-term solutions over short-term mitigations.
- Ensure performance, accessibility, and security are not regressed while fixing or implementing features.

These guidelines apply to all changes across frontend, backend, and database code.